    faqs: [["How long does a whole-house renovation take?", "It depends on the size of the house and how much structure changes, but a full renovation of a four-bedroom house, back to brick with new services, typically runs several months on site. We give you a dated programme with the cost plan and update it as the job progresses."], ["Can we live in the house during the work?", "For a full back-to-brick renovation it is usually better and cheaper to move out: the house has no services for a period and every room is a work area. For phased work we can plan around an occupied house, which we do routinely on commercial jobs."], ["Do you handle planning and Building Control?", "Internal renovation rarely needs planning permission, but extensions, loft and basement conversions and changes to a listed building or a house in a conservation area can. All structural and most services work needs Building Control approval, which we arrange and manage as part of the contract."], ["Which areas do you cover for renovations?", "Altrincham, Hale, Bowdon, Hale Barns, Timperley and Sale, and the wider Cheshire and south Manchester area including Wilmslow, Knutsford and Didsbury."]],
