    facts: [["Basement", "£3,000–£5,000 / sq m"], ["Extension", "£2,400–£3,600 / sq m"], ["Whole-house refurbishment", "£1,400–£2,800 / sq m"]],
    cardsHeading: "How a basement *gets built.*",
    cards: [["Structure and underpinning", "The existing walls are underpinned in a controlled sequence, designed by a structural engineer and inspected by Building Control as the work progresses."], ["Waterproofing", "A designed waterproofing system, typically a cavity drain membrane with sump and pump or a tanked lining, so the space stays dry for the long term."], ["Services and ventilation", "Drainage, mechanical ventilation, heating, power, lighting and data brought in while the shell is open, with escape routes designed in."], ["Finished rooms", "Cinema rooms, offices, gyms, lounges and guest suites, finished to match the rest of the house."]],
    scope: ["Structural design and underpinning", "Excavation and muck away", "Cavity drain membranes, sumps and pumps or tanked linings", "Drainage and ventilation", "Mechanical and electrical", "Staircases, partitions and finishes", "Party wall and Building Control coordination"],
    projects: ["hale-basement-conversion", "wilmslow-house"],
    faqs: [["Does a basement conversion need planning permission?", "Converting an existing cellar usually does not, as long as the outside of the house does not change and it is not a listed building. Digging a new basement, enlarging one, adding a lightwell or changing the external appearance usually does, and some Altrincham and Hale streets sit in conservation areas. We check this with you at cost-plan stage."], ["Does it need Building Regulations approval?", "Yes. Structure, waterproofing, fire escape, ventilation, damp-proofing and electrics are all covered by the Building Regulations, and the underpinning is inspected in stages. We arrange and manage this as part of the contract."], ["Will I need a party wall agreement?", "If the house is semi-detached or terraced, or the excavation is close to a neighbour's foundations, the Party Wall etc. Act 1996 almost always applies. We advise early so notices go out before the programme depends on them."], ["How much does a basement cost?", "As a 2026 working guide, £3,000–£5,000 per square metre of finished floor area, excluding VAT, professional fees and abnormals. Ground conditions, water table, access for muck away and the finish specification drive the number, so we price the actual house rather than a headline rate."]],
